libjuice 3c40a354: keep the poll worker while finished agents retain its registry

MPL-2.0, like src/conn_poll.c; original file notice preserved unchanged.
2026-10-03: J.J. Boyd (KG4VCF), with AI-assisted implementation via OpenAI Codex.

Eligible sockets and retained registry ownership are distinct. After a socket
error finishes the only agent, keep polling the existing interrupt descriptor
until the registry is empty. A later agent wakes the same worker. Preparation
errors and fatal poll errors still stop it; failed agents remain failed.
No extra worker, spin loop, timeout change or interrupt policy is introduced.

